WF-23 — Pre-Form Intent Filter

## Summary

- Inputs (WF-01 canonical envelope per data-contract-discipline Phase 1 — design.md §2.1): `phoneNumber` (E.164 string), `messageType`, `messageContent`, `user` (object or null), `pendingUser` ({id, contact_name} or null). Additional field passed by WF-02: `messageText` (free-form text for WF-25 input; note: WF-25 reads `messageContent` but callers pass `messageText` — tracked as TD-DRIFT-009, deferred from Phase 1 per §1.5), `userId`, `userStatus`.
- Outputs: For `general_enquiry` intent — a Gemini-generated WhatsApp reply tailored to the pre-form stage. For other pass-through intents — re-sends the Flow form via WF-50 with a contextual intro. For stop_intent — sends a stop-intent clarifier via WF-50. Garbage / abuse handled inside WF-25 (no return to caller). On Gemini General Response outage — sends user apology + dual admin alerts then halts via stopAndError (error propagates to WF-02 caller).
- State Transitions: none directly. Auto-opt-out on Gemini-classified stop_intent removed 2026-05-23 (SP-04) — the user must now send the explicit STOP keyword (handled by WF-20) to opt out.
- Calls Sub-Workflows: WF-25 (Intent Classifier), WF-50 (Send WhatsApp), WF-51 (Send Slack Message — admin alerts on Gemini outage).
- **Notes:**
  - **General-enquiry Gemini branch (2026-05-26 — GAP-3C):** `general_enquiry` intent now routes to a Gemini-generated contextual reply with a pre-form stage cue (gentle nudge to fill the form) and an email-callout (`chinmay_astro@gmail.com`). Other pass-through intents (wants_consultation, rebook_intent, feedback_intent) keep the existing canned flow-form re-prompt.
  - **Gemini General Response halt-and-notify (2026-05-27 — TD-PGF-09 scope expansion):** Gemini outage on `Gemini General Response` no longer silently halts the workflow. The HTTP node has `onError=continueErrorOutput`; on retries exhausted (3× with backoff), the error branch fans out to user apology (WF-50) + dual admin alerts (WF-51 to user's consult channel + admin-commands), then a `stopAndError` node terminates execution. The error propagates to WF-02's `Call WF-23` executeWorkflow node which halts the caller (no `onError` continueErrorOutput on the caller side per Decision #2 — sub-workflow errors propagate naturally). Admin alert text: "AI assistant couldn't generate a reply" (vs WF-25's classifier-failure copy). Pre-form fallback: when `user.slack_channel_id` is null/empty (typical for WF-23's pre-onboarding stage), the consult-channel alert is skipped — only `chinmay-admin-commands` receives the notification. User-apology + admin-alert copy locked 2026-05-27T02:25:00Z (sprint state TD-PGF-09 §Approved user/admin copy).
  - **stop_intent policy (2026-05-23 — SP-04, applying WF-40's TD-E pattern):** Gemini-classified stop_intent no longer auto-routes to WF-47 unsubscribe — false-positive risk on pre-onboarding text. Instead WF-23 sends a clarifier asking the user to send STOP exactly if they want to opt out; otherwise the next message proceeds normally through WF-02 routing. Literal STOP keyword still goes through WF-20 (Design Rule #5) and unsubscribes canonically.
  - WF-23 passes `messageText` into WF-25, but WF-25's `Prepare Intent Request` reads `input.messageContent`. Latent bug tracked as TD-DRIFT-009 — explicitly deferred from Phase 1 per §1.5. If the field is undefined, the Gemini prompt may classify on an empty string.
  - **Provably dead-code branch removed 2026-05-23 (SP-04):** the previous `Is Stop Intent?` IF's FALSE branch was unreachable — `Is Pass-Through Intent?` already excludes garbage/abusive/inappropriate (which never return from WF-25 anyway) and stop_intent, so anything reaching the inner IF was stop_intent. Direct connection used now.
  - **Call WF-25 envelope add-on (2026-05-27 — TD-PGF-05):** caller-side `workflowInputs.value` mapping extended from 4 fields (phoneNumber, userId, messageText, userStatus) to 6 fields, adding `userName` (from `user.name || pendingUser.contact_name`) and `slackChannelId` (from `user.slack_channel_id`) per data-contract-discipline (memory: feedback_data_contract_discipline). WF-25 reads these directly for its own halt-and-notify alert template — no DB lookup added inside WF-25. Pre-form users have null slack_channel_id; passes through cleanly.

---

## Algorithm

Step 1: Start — workflow triggered by another workflow (WF-02) with WF-01 canonical envelope plus `messageText`, `userId`, `userStatus`. Read `phoneNumber` from top-level envelope field (canonical per §2.1).
Step 2: Call WF-25 (Intent Classifier) with 6 fields: phoneNumber, userId, messageText, userStatus, userName (from `user.name || pendingUser.contact_name`), slackChannelId (from `user.slack_channel_id`). WF-25 returns intentResult ∈ {wants_consultation, general_enquiry, rebook_intent, feedback_intent, stop_intent} for non-terminal intents. Note: for garbage / malicious_abusive / inappropriate, WF-25 sends warnings + auto-blocks before returning control (effectively a halt for those intents). Note: WF-25 may itself halt-and-notify on its own Gemini outage; that halt propagates here and on to WF-02.
Step 3: Check `Is Pass-Through Intent?` — is the intent NOT one of {garbage, malicious_abusive, inappropriate, stop_intent}?
  - If YES (pass-through — wants_consultation, general_enquiry, rebook_intent, feedback_intent) → GOTO Step 4
  - If NO (intentResult == stop_intent — only reachable value here per WF-25 contract) → GOTO Step 19
Step 4: Check `Is General Enquiry?` — is intentResult == "general_enquiry"?
  - If YES → GOTO Step 5
  - If NO → GOTO Step 17
Step 5: Build Gemini prompt instructing a helpful, warm assistant for Chinmay's Vedic astrology consultation service on WhatsApp, with the user-stage cue "user has not yet completed our intake form" and the email-callout cue "they can email chinmay_astro@gmail.com for anything else". Ask Gemini to weave both naturally into a brief 2-3 sentence reply in plain conversational English (no bullet lists, no robotic phrasing). Append the user's messageContent.
Step 6: POST to Gemini (gemini-2.5-flash-lite per project standard — see project_gemini_model memory) with temperature=0.3 (low for response stability), maxOutputTokens=200, timeout=10s, retryOnFail=true, maxTries=3, onError=continueErrorOutput. On success (main output): GOTO Step 7. On retries exhausted (error output): GOTO Step 8 (halt-and-notify chain).
Step 7: Extract Gemini reply text from candidates[0].content.parts[0].text; fallback default "Thank you for your message! For questions about our Vedic astrology consultation, feel free to ask." Call WF-50 with { phoneNumber, messageType="text", messageContent=reply } per §2.3 canonical contract. End.
Step 8: Build user apology WF-50 payload per §2.3 — { phoneNumber: `$('When Executed by Another Workflow').item.json.phoneNumber`, messageType="text", messageContent="Sorry — we ran into a brief technical issue and couldn't process your message just now. Dr. Chinmay has been notified and will follow up with you shortly. We apologise for the inconvenience." }.
Step 9: Call WF-50 (apology to user). Continue to admin alert chain (Step 10).
Step 10: Build admin alert text (Code node) — translate userStatus to plain English (payment_pending → "awaiting payment approval"; consultation_active → "in active consultation"; consultation_closed → "consultation completed"; payment_submitted → "payment under review"; blocked → "blocked"; opted_out → "opted out"; default / pre-form → "filling onboarding form"). Resolve userName = `user.name || pendingUser.contact_name || phoneNumber`. Construct messageText: "⚠️ The AI assistant couldn't generate a reply to a user just now.\n\n*User:* {userName} ({phoneNumber})\n*Their state:* {stateText}\n*Their question:* \"{messageContent truncated to 500 chars}\"\n*Reason:* {error summary truncated to 200 chars}\n\nThe user has been told there's a technical hiccup and that you'll follow up. Suggested action: respond manually in their consult channel." Emit { messageText }.
Step 11: Check `Has Consult Channel?` — is `user.slack_channel_id` non-empty (notEmpty unary operator)?
  - If YES → GOTO Step 12 (consult-channel alert path, then admin-commands alert).
  - If NO (pre-form user with no consult channel) → GOTO Step 14 (admin-commands alert only).
Step 12: Build consult alert payload per §2.5 — { channelId: `$('When Executed by Another Workflow').item.json.user.slack_channel_id`, messageText: `$('Build Admin Alert Text').item.json.messageText` }.
Step 13: Call WF-51 (consult-channel alert). GOTO Step 14.
Step 14: Build admin-commands alert payload per §2.5 — { channelId: "C0A5B0ZE81E" (chinmay-admin-commands), messageText: `$('Build Admin Alert Text').item.json.messageText` }.
Step 15: Call WF-51 (admin-commands alert). GOTO Step 16.
Step 16: stopAndError — terminate WF-23 execution with errorMessage "Gemini general response failed; user apology + admin alerts dispatched. Halting execution so caller propagates termination." n8n's executeWorkflow error-propagation contract halts WF-02 at its `Call WF-23` node.
Step 17: (pass-through non-general-enquiry path — from Step 4 NO branch) Build a contextual intro line based on intentResult:
  - "wants_consultation" → "Great! Please fill in your birth details to book your Vedic astrology consultation with Chinmay."
  - Otherwise (rebook_intent, feedback_intent) → "To proceed with your consultation, please fill in your birth details using the form below."
  Append the privacy policy URL. Build the interactive Flow payload (type=flow, header="Birth Details Form", flowId="1408011897720771", flowCta="Fill Details").
Step 18: Call WF-50 with { phoneNumber, messageType="interactive", interactivePayload=the flow object } per §2.3 canonical contract. End.
Step 19: (stop_intent path — from Step 3 NO branch) Build WF-50 stop-intent clarifier payload per §2.3 canonical contract:
  - phoneNumber = <phoneNumber> (from top-level envelope)
  - messageType = "text"
  - messageContent = "This is an automated message from Chinmay Astro — we noticed your message mentioned STOP or unsubscribing. If this was unrelated, please ignore. If you do want to opt out of this service, simply send STOP at any time."
Step 20: Call WF-50 (Stop Clarifier) with the prepared payload. End.
